# Print which reviews this branch owes, before it becomes a PR.
#
# Reporting, not blocking: nothing here can tell whether a review actually
# happened, only which ones the table in CLAUDE.md requires. The point is that
# the answer arrives unprompted. The rule was "non-trivial changes get
# reviewed" and was violated seven PRs running; it became a table, and the
# table was then skipped three more times — because running the grep was still
# something a person had to remember.
#
# `|| ...` rather than a bare call because this must not block a push. But a
# bare `|| true` swallowed the exit code: `blastRadius()` throws when it cannot
# find the list in docs/GIT.md, and because the headline prints first, stdout
# read as an ordinary short run with no triggers owed. Measured — reword the
# heading and all four rows and the summary vanish, exit 0.
#
# Not silent, to be exact: node's stack trace goes to stderr and git relays it,
# and an earlier version of this comment claimed otherwise. What `|| true` cost
# was the exit code and the report, next to which a trace scrolling past during
# a push is easy to miss. Under-reporting is the one direction this tool must
# never fail in, so the failure now says so on stdout, where the report is.
node tools/review-triggers.ts ||
  echo "  !!  review-triggers FAILED — which reviews are owed is UNKNOWN. Run 'pnpm review-triggers'."
